<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Under the Crop Residue Management \(CRM\) initiative, efforts during the quarter focused on reducing stubble burning and promoting practical, sustainable alternatives for farmers. 28 villages had been identified based on high residue-burning incidence and limited access to agricultural machinery. A survey of 311 farmers was conducted, with approximately 90% providing consent to participate in CRM interventions. Through in-situ CRM interventions, 1,423 acres of farmland were protected from residue burning during the reporting period. In addition, 16,800+ quintals of chaff were collected and supplied to end-user industries, creating a productive use pathway for crop residue.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
