/P 87 0 R
/E (Mahavir Singh Hada previously practiced traditional farming methods on his 50-bigha agricultural land. During the Kharif season, he followed conventional paddy transplanting practices. After harvesting wheat, he used to burn the leftover crop residue in the field. This practice negatively affected soil fertility made the soil increasingly hard and adversely impacted overall soil health and biological quality. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (After associating with Roots Foundation, Mahavir Singh Hada introduced significant changes in his farming practices. Instead of conventional paddy transplanting, he adopted Direct Seeded Rice \(DSR\) technology with the support of a Step Seeder machine. This helped reduce the requirement for time, labour, and irrigation, making paddy cultivation more efficient, scientific, and sustainable.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
